{
  "reason": "Use Tier 2: separate context and candidate item representations. The uniform preference branch produced the best observed HR@10 of 0.5375, while subsequent recency and hard-negative changes declined to 0.4838; this motivates a representation change rather than further sampling or weighting adjustments. Shared embeddings must simultaneously encode history preferences and distinguish candidate items, creating potentially conflicting gradients; untied embeddings directly test this hypothesis without repeating earlier experiments.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Introduce a separate trainable output_emb embedding table in SASRec for candidate scoring, retaining item_emb exclusively for Transformer inputs and preference pooling; this Tier 2 change separates contextual similarity from next-item discrimination. Initialize output_emb by copying item_emb immediately after its existing initialization, zero its padding row, and replace candidate embedding lookups in positive scoring, detached hard-negative mining, differentiable negative rescoring, and predict with output_emb while retaining item_bias. Preserve SASRec's existing constructor arguments and forward(self, seq), ranking_loss(self, seq, pos, negative), and predict(self, seq, candidates) signatures, adding only an optional trailing untied_output=True configuration argument. Keep the current preference pooling, gate, loss weighting, 144-negative sampler, mining procedure, optimizer, and hyperparameters unchanged so this experiment isolates embedding-role separation.",
    "training_evaluation": "Save untied_output=True in train_one metadata and update PREDICTOR and its writer to reconstruct the same architecture and strictly load output_emb for every dataset. Replace obsolete diagnostic expectations with checks that the two tables initially match but have independent storage, both receive finite training gradients, mining and prediction use output_emb, and generated-predictor scores agree with checkpoint-reloaded validation scores. Preserve supplied splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four category routes, trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution, the 200-epoch environment default, and existing runtime limits. Evaluate with the unchanged 200-user, 99-unique-negative, seed-42 validation protocol and checkpoint selection, comparing host macro HR@10 against the immediate 0.4838 reference and historical 0.5375 best without claiming improvement before measurement. Retain the final validation-score print and host-managed held-out inference without reading hidden test files or fabricating a submission."
  }
